        "original_id": "2af3e01a-63ae-553c-a512-9dbd6e167c71",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 79 Pall Mall, Pall Mall, London\n- People: Nell Gwyn, King Charles II of England and Scotland\n- Concepts: Grade II listed buildings, blue plaques\n\nFacts:\n- Nell Gwyn, also spelled Gwynn or Gwynne, was born on 2 February 1650 and died on 14 November 1687.\n- Nell Gwyn was a long-time mistress of King Charles II of England and Scotland.\n- A brick townhouse formerly stood on the site of 79 Pall Mall, and Nell Gwyn occupied that townhouse after her retirement from the stage.\n- A blue plaque at 79 Pall Mall notes Nell Gwyn’s former residence on the site.\n- 79 Pall Mall is a Grade II listed building on Pall Mall in London.",
